hexagony programs vendored for integration testing
====================================================

the `.in` files in this directory are hexagony programs sourced
verbatim from the `examples/` directory of the upstream hexagony
repository:

  https://github.com/m-ender/hexagony
  copy is at internal/integrationtest/testdata/gems/hexagony/

each `.in` is the corresponding `<name>.hxg` from `examples/`,
renamed so the goruby esolang test harness (which globs `*.in`)
picks them up. the sibling `.expected` files were generated by
running the multi-file interpreter

  ruby internal/integrationtest/testdata/gems/hexagony/interpreter.rb \
       <fixture>.in </dev/null > <fixture>.expected

under MRI 2.6.10.

omitted programs and why
------------------------

- prime.hxg -- doesn't terminate under empty stdin (it's a
  prime-checking program expecting numeric input). prime-compact
  and prime-small print 0 immediately (their entry path under
  empty stdin returns) and are vendored as fixtures.

